# Docs + headers must track architecture changes

When you **move responsibilities**, **rename/delete modules**, or **change load order**, update architecture docs and touched module headers in the same change set.

## Required updates when architecture changes

- **Load order**: `CombatMode/Embeds.xml` (new modules before their consumers) and `STRUCTURE.md`.
- **Module map / durable notes**: `.cursor/rules/combatmode-architecture-and-style.mdc`.
- **Agent index**: `AGENTS.md` only if the rule map or finish flow changed (keep it thin — no duplicated module encyclopedia).
- **File headers**: for any edited/added `CombatMode/**.lua`, use this **default** header shape (every file, not only large ones):
  - title line: `Path/File.lua — DOMAIN — short title`
  - **What it does:** purpose/behavior in plain language
  - **Architecture / how it works:** mechanics, DB keys, events, public APIs, gotchas
  - **Does not:** responsibilities left to other modules
  - **Related:** sibling modules for cross-feature work (callers, DB, events, options)

## Keep behavior stable by default

- Prefer **API-preserving moves**: keep existing `CM.*` function names and global handlers unless explicitly requested.
- If behavior changes are intended, call them out and update docs accordingly.
